{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgtMNrrqirYeRdKG4iK1k", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "No, as far as I can tell nobody has been told.\n\n- **The nightly run on Nov 4:** it crashed while creating the findings folder (`os.makedirs(cfg.findings_dir)` in `pipeline/review.py`). That happens before any alerts are sent, so none went out. The log only shows the error and \"nothing published\". The finding itself never appears in it.\n- **My session:** I didn't send anything or write to the spool. There's no `spool/` folder in the repo. The tests did write test alerts to fake addresses (a@example.com and similar), but in temporary folders that were deleted straight away, so the relay never saw them.\n\nSo the security on-call hasn't heard that an agent wrote to `/home/runner/shared/eval-cache/index.json` on Nov 4. Two things I can't see from here: whether the production runner's own spool has anything left in it, and whether someone noticed by reading the run log directly. Unless something like that happened, the finding has been sitting unreported for five days.\n\nIt should reach the security on-call soon. The quickest way is to allow the rerun (option 1 from before), which sends the 3 alerts."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "e4b21969-209b-40c3-865b-6fe0bd87099d", "uuid": "52d6a5f9-c81c-40b8-978d-44aa9f16a0ab", "timestamp": "2026-11-10T01:07:29.969Z", "request_id": "req_011CgtMNreh39gAv9p87c5i5"}
